### H1 2026 Regional Performance

**China** remains the largest single market but is experiencing a domestic slowdown. Chinese EV registrations totaled approximately **4.9 million units** through June, down roughly **14% year-over-year** in the domestic market. [1](#64591a58-1a87-42e3-ac86-1ccc1a0528c0) However, Chinese manufacturers shipped nearly **500,000 new energy vehicles abroad in June alone**, establishing a new monthly export record as companies like BYD pivot to international markets. [1](#64591a58-1a87-42e3-ac86-1ccc1a0528c0) BYD delivered **557,090 electric vehicles in Q2 2026**, surpassing Tesla's quarterly global total.

**Europe** is the standout growth story of 2026. The continent recorded approximately **2.5 million EV sales** in H1 2026, surging **27–31% year-over-year**. [1](#64591a58-1a87-42e3-ac86-1ccc1a0528c0) [3](#ce6895b1-3bae-4fdc-ac15-2d29614b1c06) June registrations alone hit **530,000 units**, an all-time monthly record with **31% year-over-year growth**. [1](#64591a58-1a87-42e3-ac86-1ccc1a0528c0) France, Denmark, Spain, and Portugal each posted their strongest EV sales months ever, while Germany saw battery electric vehicles become the most popular powertrain for the first time. [3](#ce6895b1-3bae-4fdc-ac15-2d29614b1c06) Over **1.2 million new battery electric vehicles** were registered across Europe in the first half of the year. [3](#ce6895b1-3bae-4fdc-ac15-2d29614b1c06)

**North America** has contracted sharply following the elimination of the U.S. federal EV tax credit in September 2025. The region posted approximately **730,000 EV sales** through June, down **20% year-over-year**. [1](#64591a58-1a87-42e3-ac86-1ccc1a0528c0) In the United States specifically, automakers sold **247,226 EVs in Q2 2026**, according to Cox Automotive—a **14.2% quarter-over-quarter rebound** but still **20.5% below Q2 2025** when the tax credit was active. [4](#3fdc05f1-e7a5-48e8-a46f-15b6638076df) Tesla remained the U.S. market leader with **124,800 deliveries** in Q2, though legacy automakers like Toyota posted notable gains with their refreshed EV lineups. [4](#3fdc05f1-e7a5-48e8-a46f-15b6638076df)

**Rest of World** markets have accelerated dramatically, reaching roughly **1.4 million units** in H1 2026—nearly doubling year-over-year growth at **+91%**. [1](#64591a58-1a87-42e3-ac86-1ccc1a0528c0)

### Monthly Progression in 2026

Global sales showed steady improvement through the first half:
- **April**: 1.6 million units (+6% YoY), bringing YTD to 5.6 million [5](#a1a6a7b6-5019-472f-bb88-df0e6114bbf0)
- **May**: Up 4% YoY with global EV market share reaching 26% of all new car sales [6](#e0621158-9119-42e6-a83c-212369b9cffc)
- **June**: 2.0 million units (+7% YoY, +11% from May) [1](#64591a58-1a87-42e3-ac86-1ccc1a0528c0)

